<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2024-memory-03--grok> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7 on levin-2024-memory-03: not-empirically-resolvable, resolvability 0.06";
    dc:description "The text presents this as a way memories could be seen on a processual view of mind. No measurement of neural, cellular, or network activity distinguishes an agential memory from a pattern being transformed by the system that stores it. The claim is not an empirical proposition that current data could settle.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Treating a memory trace as a minimally agential participant in its own reinterpretation does not specify an observation that would differ from ordinary dynamics of an excitable medium.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Agency of a pattern is not separable from the dynamics of the medium that carries it.", "The claim is explicitly a speculation about how to see memories.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.9"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.06"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "not-empirically-resolvable".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2024-memory-03--grok--analysis-feasibility> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
